An object-mode Transform that groups input into arrays of exactly `size`,
emitting a final short batch from `_flush`.

```ts
// in:  1, 2, 3, 4, 5     size 2
// out: [1, 2], [3, 4], [5]

// in:  1, 2, 3, 4        size 2
// out: [1, 2], [3, 4]    — no trailing empty array

// in:  nothing
// out: nothing           — an empty stream emits no batches at all
```

`size` must be a positive integer; anything else throws from `createBatcher`
itself, before a stream exists.

The gate collects the emitted batches, mutates the first one, and then checks
that the second is unaffected — a transform that reuses one array and pushes it
repeatedly emits the same object every time and fails this.

```
