```

Reimplement the promise form of `pipeline` without using `stream.pipeline` or
`stream/promises`. `stream.finished` and `pipe` are allowed.

Required behaviour, each of which the gate tests separately:

- data flows through every stage with backpressure intact;
- the promise resolves only when the **last** stage has finished and closed;
- an error in **any** stage rejects with that error;
- when any stage fails, every other stage is destroyed — including the ones
  upstream of the failure, which is the direction `pipe` never looks;
- when several stages fail, the **first** error is the one reported;
- a stage destroyed without an error rejects with an
  `ERR_STREAM_PREMATURE_CLOSE`-style error;
- fewer than two streams throws immediately.

```ts
await myPipeline(Readable.from(["a"]), upper, sink);
sinkContents();                                  // "A"

const bad = new Transform({ transform(_c, _e, cb) { cb(new Error("nope")); } });
await myPipeline(src, bad, sink).catch((e) => e.message);   // "nope"
src.destroyed && sink.destroyed;                            // true
```

