## Problem 5 — a tree that does not fit in memory

Edit `ex5/solution.ts`. Implement:

```ts
export function walk(root: string): AsyncGenerator<string>;
```

Yield the path of every regular file beneath `root`, **relative to `root`**,
using `opendir` so that a directory with a million entries is streamed rather
than materialised.

```ts
// root/
//   a.txt
//   sub/b.txt
//   sub/link -> ../a.txt
for await (const p of walk(root)) console.log(p);
// "a.txt"
// "sub/b.txt"      (path.sep on Windows)
// the symlink is NOT yielded and NOT followed
```

Requirements:

- symlinks are skipped entirely — a link to an ancestor directory is an
  infinite walk and a link out of the tree is a boundary crossed;
- directories are descended, in the order `opendir` supplies;
- a directory that cannot be read (`EACCES`) is skipped rather than aborting
  the whole walk, but any other error propagates;
- `root` itself missing propagates `ENOENT`;
- an empty tree yields nothing.

The gate builds a tree containing a symlink loop and asserts the walk
terminates.

```
uv run dojo test node v3na05_fs_handles_atomic ex5
```

references.solution.ts:
// v3na05_fs_handles_atomic / ex5 - reference solution (author only, used by `dojo verify`).
import { opendir } from "node:fs/promises";
import { join, relative } from "node:path";

export async function* walk(root: string): AsyncGenerator<string> {
  yield* walkFrom(root, root);
}

async function* walkFrom(root: string, dirPath: string): AsyncGenerator<string> {
  let dir;
  try {
    // opendir streams entries; readdir would materialise a million Dirents
    // before the first line of logic runs.
    dir = await opendir(dirPath);
  } catch (err) {
    // An unreadable directory is skipped, not fatal: a walk over / as a
    // non-root user hits dozens. Anything else is a real problem.
    if ((err as NodeJS.ErrnoException).code === "EACCES") return;
    throw err;
  }

  for await (const entry of dir) {
    const full = join(dirPath, entry.name);

    // Symlink test FIRST, explicitly. Dirent uses lstat semantics, so a link
    // to a directory reports isDirectory() === false and this would "work"
    // even reordered - but then correctness depends on a fact the next reader
    // has to know, and a loop into an ancestor never terminates.
    if (entry.isSymbolicLink()) continue;

    if (entry.isDirectory()) {
      yield* walkFrom(root, full);
    } else if (entry.isFile()) {
      yield relative(root, full);
    }
    // Sockets, FIFOs and devices are deliberately neither yielded nor entered.
  }
}

