## Problem 4 — hash without a second pass

Edit `ex4/solution.ts`. Implement:

```ts
export interface HashingStream {
  stream: Transform;
  digest(): Buffer;      // throws until the stream has finished
  bytes(): number;
}

export function createHashingPassThrough(algorithm: string): HashingStream;
```

A stage that is transparent to the data and computes its hash in flight.

```ts
const h = createHashingPassThrough("sha256");
await pipeline(Readable.from(["hello ", "world"]), h.stream, sink);
h.digest().toString("hex");
// "b94d27b9934d3e08a52e52d7da7dabfac484efe37a5380ee9088f7ace2efcde9"
h.bytes();       // 11
sinkContents();  // "hello world"
```

Requirements:

- chunk boundaries are preserved — one chunk in, the same chunk out;
- `digest()` before the stream has finished throws an `Error` mentioning
  `not finished`, rather than returning a hash of a prefix;
- `digest()` is callable repeatedly and returns the same value;
- an unknown algorithm throws from the factory, not from the first write.

The gate hashes a 10 MB stream and compares against `createHash` over the same
bytes, and separately asserts that calling `digest()` mid-stream throws.

